WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Global Benchmarks for World-Class Quality

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome back to this session on benchmarking.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.766
What we’re looking at now is the Sigma Scale one sigma, two, three, four, and so on.

4
00:00:12.766 --> 00:00:17.632
And the corresponding percentages associated with each.

5
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:23.066
So, what we’re looking at is about 1.5 Sigma is about 50% good.

6
00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:26.866
2.3. Sigma is about 80% good.

7
00:00:26.866 --> 00:00:30.866
90% is 2.8. 99 is about 3.8.

8
00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:35.632
99.9 is about 4.6 Sigma.

9
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:40.199
99.99% good stuff is 5.2.

10
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.333
Three 9’s is 5.8 Sigma.

11
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:49.199
So, we can clearly see from this chart

12
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:55.933
that 99.9%, 4.6 Sigma,

13
00:00:55.933 --> 00:01:01.233
is generally around best in class. World-class Five Sigma.

14
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:07.266
The typical service organization is around 2.5 Sigma,

15
00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:11.299
while the target for manufacturing is about Four Sigma.

16
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:18.066
And recall that, that translates to roughly 20% of sales.

17
00:01:18.066 --> 00:01:24.232
Whereas Six Sigma, or 3.4 defects per million opportunities, is less than 1% of sales.

18
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:28.566
So, this allows us to see what our competitive advantage might be

19
00:01:28.566 --> 00:01:31.732
when comparing ourselves to someone else.

20
00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:34.833
Remember from our previous benchmarking

21
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:38.566
We take the notion, Y is a function of X.

22
00:01:38.566 --> 00:01:43.232
So, if I see something on the outcome, that's about Four Sigma.

23
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:48.166
What do you suppose I surmise about that Four Sigma?

24
00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:54.766
Basically, Four Sigma in. Four Sigma out.

25
00:01:54.766 --> 00:02:01.766
So, If I take Four Sigma drawings, Four Sigma managers, Four Sigma trained people,

26
00:02:01.766 --> 00:02:07.099
Four Sigma suppliers. What do you suppose comes out the back end?

27
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.433
Twenty Sigma? I don't think so.

28
00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:13.399
Trash in. Trash out. Average in. Average out.

29
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.666
So, this is another form of benchmarking.

30
00:02:17.666 --> 00:02:22.666
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
